          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Consequences of the Agreement</strong><br>\nOne of the consequences of the Oslo Accords was the establishment of the Palestinian Authority, which had a degree of self-rule in certain areas. However, ongoing tensions and conflicts meant that the hoped-for progress towards peace was not achieved.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Obstacles and Challenges</strong><br>\nThe Oslo Accords faced many obstacles and challenges, including ongoing violence, Israel's settlement policy, and disagreements over the final status solution. These factors contributed to the original goal of achieving lasting peace not being met.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Lessons from the Oslo Accords</strong><br>\nThe Oslo Accords teach us that the peace process in the Middle East is complex and challenging. It also shows that despite good intentions and significant efforts from both sides, resolving long-standing conflicts requires time, patience, and a genuine willingness to cooperate.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
